WEBVTT

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:12.320
Say, how do you like my face?

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.570
Pretty disgusting, isn't it?

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.280
It's pitiful, isn't it?

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:20.250
It's <i>amazing</i>, right?

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:24.870
You know, I was trying to ruin Iona,
so it was <i>my</i> face that ended up being ruined...

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.130
I was trying to end her career as a model, you know,

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.760
but it's <i>my</i> career that's over now...

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.430
It's funny, isn't it?

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.720
It makes you laugh, doesn't it?

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:43.560
So...

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.100
laugh!

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:46.230
Ruuko!

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:50.780
This is how super-cute Aki-lucky's face looks now!

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:53.150
Come on, take a look! Ain't I just pathetic?

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.110
Quit it, Akira!

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.530
It's your fault.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:02.700
I lost to you...

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.500
And that's why I'm stuck with this face now.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.500
So, now...

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.880
Yours, and yours, and Iona's...

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.220
I'm gonna make all of your faces look like mine!

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.220
What are you girls doing there?!

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.550
Stop!

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.970
You girls wait here!

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:25.270
Let's get away from here, Ruuko.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:26.440
O-Okay.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:38.780
She's not chasing us...

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.030
Y-Yeah...

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.410
I'm glad...

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:45.870
There's nothing to be glad about...

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.000
Akira-san is right.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.090
It's my fault that Akira-san is...

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:53.670
Ruuko...

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.550
If you really don't have a wish,
you should quit while you still can, Ruuko.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.640
Quit. Your grandma will be sad if something happens to you.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.650
I'm not the only one who
should quit! You should, too!

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.570
If you lose, then your family...

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:16.820
Kazuki-kun would be heartbroken, too!

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.780
I'm not going to quit.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:23.450
Yuzuki...

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.410
You saw what happened to Akira-san!

00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:28.160
I won't end up like her.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.080
But... why...

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:34.250
Ruuko, I'm sorry to make you worry.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:35.210
Yuzuki?

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.550
But I can't quit now.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.970
I almost gave up on my impossible wish...

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:44.510
But now it's right before my eyes.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.230
Let's not be friends anymore.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:50.900
I'm going to become an Eternal Girl.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.110
And if you're with me when that happens,

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:56.320
you'll always be burdened
by the sad memories you'll make.

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.530
W-Wait...

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.150
I'm sorry.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.120
Wait, Yuzuki!

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:05.370
Ruuko!

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.870
I really had fun with you!

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.830
I'll treasure my matching scrunchie forever!

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.000
Yuzuki...

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.340
Next time we meet, I'll be a new Yuzuki!

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.760
I'll be Kazuki's girlfriend!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:47.410
shinjitsu wa hitoe ni kaado no uraomote
Truth and reality are like the two sides of a card

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:52.920
tokenai mama
Forever entwined

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.670
mekurimekuru meku
Thrust upon this chaotic stage

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:01.670
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.930
memagurushii suteeji de
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way
I spin around and lose my way

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:10.980
sono karamatta kanjou wo manzoku iku made nankai mo
Until I can finally sort out these mixed-up emotions

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.230
kowashite shimae
I'll destroy it countless times

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:19.320
unmei ni temaneki sare samayou ashita wa
The uncertain future will be summoned by fate

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:24.610
nani wo erande nani wo tebanashi hitotsu ni nareba iin darou
Should I choose just one thing to let go of?

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:30.370
najitta tefuda wo sarasu yoyuu nante nai yo
I can't afford to let my sinful hand show yet

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:35.460
kawaita koukai no umi wo nomihosu hibi wa
My days of leisurely drinking from the sea of regret are long over

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:40.800
kagirareta kotoba de itsushika no egao yurushite hoshiin darou
Will you really use your one wish to return that lost smile?

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:47.010
utsutsu wo wasuretatte kamawanai yo dakara
It's no concern of mine if you avert your eyes from reality

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:51.770
ima wa shiranai de itai nee
So please just live in blissful ignorance

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.710
Ruu? Ruu?

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.670
Ruu...?

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:29.600
Ruuko!

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.310
Where in the world have you been?

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:34.600
At least give us a call
if you're going to be this late!

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.690
That's none of your business.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.570
It may be none of my business.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:45.780
But...

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.030
you still shouldn't do anything to make Grandma worry.

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.450
Ruuko?

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:54.580
Is Grandma home?

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.370
Yeah. Hurry up and go see her.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.560
I'm back...

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.150
Welcome home, Ruu-chan.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.320
Icy, icy!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.820
I just made some warm amazake.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.700
I figured Ruu-chan would come home all cold.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.240
Now, come on in.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.160
Why...

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:41.670
Why aren't you asking me anything, Grandma?

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:47.630
We'll talk when you want to talk.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.680
Is that all right with you?

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:02.480
<b>Ruuko
Ruuko
Ruuko</b>

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.020
Ruu?

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:07.650
Did the amazake taste good?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.360
Are you asleep?

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:18.120
You know, Tama likes when Ruu is having fun battling.

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:20.830
But...

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.670
I don't like to...

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.300
see you sad.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.470
Morning, Kazuki!

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.680
You made this, Yuzuki?

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:43.520
Well, yeah. Turns out I <i>can</i> make stuff like that.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.650
Here's some soup, too.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.320
I'm glad...

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:50.990
About what?

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:54.570
You went straight to sleep
when you came home last night.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:55.620
I was worried about you.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:59.700
Girls have days like that. Don't you forget it!

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:00.960
Sounds inconvenient.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:02.370
Come on now, time to eat.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.000
Right. Thanks.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:14.720
Tastes great!

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.770
The last time you made French toast, the eggs were still raw.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:23.020
Well... I tend to rush things.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.480
I kind of lose my cool a lot.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.980
Calm down, and wait for the right timing.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.860
Set your eyes on your goal.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.570
As long as I don't get lost on my way, things will be fine.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:37.530
Right.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.790
Meeting up with your friends?

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.250
Ah, yeah.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.000
I'll be back soon, though.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.330
Got it.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.960
I'll make dinner tonight.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.080
Really?

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:51.670
What would be good? We had French toast this morning...

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.380
Curry udon!
Curry udon!

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.970
I know everything about you, Kazuki.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:03.770
All right, I'm going.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.270
Have fun!

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:21.290
<i>Hitoe... I'm sorry.</i>

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.290
<i>I...</i>

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.290
<i>I won't end up like you.</i>

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.310
<i>I will make my wish come true.</i>

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.770
Welcome.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:04.870
That...

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.830
Did you write that?

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:17.380
Isn't it a bit dangerous to look for opponents with that method?

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.550
It probably is.

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:23.680
I don't have an issue with that,
but other Selectors may get upset.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.350
Even my LRIG is questioning what you did.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:26.640
No Entry

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:27.520
Okay.
No Entry

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:28.310
No Entry

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.770
I don't really want to battle more than I need to.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:34.150
Guess I'll finish it with this one.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:34.650
Huh?

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.400
With this battle,

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:39.280
I'll make my wish come true.

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:41.660
You're pretty confident, aren't you?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.910
Okay. Let's start.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:46.910
Open!
Open!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.800
I'm probably going first.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.010
I wonder why.

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:07.680
Things feel different today.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:08.480
Yuzuki...

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.640
Let's go, Hanayo-san!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:18.490
I see where her confidence is coming from.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.860
<i>I was wrong all along.</i>

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:25.080
<i>That's what people made me think.</i>

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.040
<i>A love that isn't allowed.</i>

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:34.340
<i>I mean, I feel so sorry for Kazuki-kun when I see him being stalked by you.</i>

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:37.170
<i>A feeling that isn't allowed.</i>

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:40.340
<i>How lewd! That's just </i>too<i> pervy!</i>

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:45.180
Spell! Severing Steamroll!

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:47.850
Direct damage!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.020
<i>I'm not wrong.</i>

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.230
<i>I'll turn everything on its head.</i>

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.780
<i>I'll turn this world where my feelings aren't allowed on its head.</i>

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:06.120
I'll be by Kazuki's side!

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.040
Yuzuki.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:17.750
Dang, I lost...

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.380
You're so good, Kazuki-kun!

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.090
Guess there's no beating you...

00:12:22.220 --> 00:12:24.470
All right, it's my turn now.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.220
I'm not gonna lose to <i>you</i> at least!

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.600
Hey, can you take a look at my deck?

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:29.260
Sure.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.480
You're running a red deck?

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.980
Yup. The SIGNI with the gem theme is really cute.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.860
Yuzuki uses a red deck, too.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.230
I feel like drinking something.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:44.110
Excuse me, is it okay if I bring a drink in?

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.360
Sure, go ahead.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.330
Kazuki-kun, can you come with me?

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.540
Hey, the vending machine...

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:58.750
Can you follow me?

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:06.180
Huh?

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:08.890
I'm sorry to spring this on you.

00:13:08.890 --> 00:13:13.230
But I really need to tell you how I feel.

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.390
I...

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:17.560
want to be with you.

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:23.190
Um... I'm not really looking for anything like that right now.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.740
Sorry.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:30.830
Is there someone else you like?

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.540
That's not it.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:37.580
Would Yuzuki-san happen to be the reason?

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.170
You're always with her!

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:43.050
What else can we do but get suspicious about you two!

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:46.930
Wh-What are you saying?
What do you mean by "suspicious"?

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:49.340
Like, doing it even though you're brother and sister!

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:53.140
That's what everyone is saying!

00:13:54.890 --> 00:13:56.140
Who's this "everyone"?

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.770
Who's spewing stuff like that? Tell me!

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:01.820
That's so rude...

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:04.490
Don't you feel sorry for Yuzuki?!

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:08.950
Tell me! Who is it? Matsumoto-san? Senda-san?!

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.410
I'll go tell them all they're wrong! Now tell me!

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.700
You're usually so kind...

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:17.120
But when it's about Yuzuki-san, you lose your temper.

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:18.210
Stop it!

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.340
Prove it to me if you think I'm wrong!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.130
Prove it to you...?

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.130
Kiss me.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:27.590
Why should I...

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.300
You don't even have to go out with me!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.470
But you can kiss me at least, right?

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:34.640
If you can't kiss me, it means you must love Yuzuki-san!

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:36.350
Isn't that right?!

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.140
This is crazy.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:41.650
Wait, Kazuki-kun!

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.360
<i>It really does feel different.</i>

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:47.780
I summon Cannon! I use its effect to banish Hass!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:54.330
<i>I feel a burning sensation inside of me,</i>

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:58.460
<i>but the very core of my body is surprisingly cold.</i>

00:14:58.460 --> 00:14:59.920
<i>Maybe that means...</i>

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.420
This battle really will be...

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:08.720
Yuzuki, I'll ask you once again—no, one last time.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:10.430
Hanayo-san?

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:14.220
If you win this battle,

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:16.680
the wish you hold dear will come true.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.770
Are you sure about this?

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:28.440
When I saw what happened to Hitoe, I blamed you.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:29.530
But I...

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.780
Even if I had been told the truth from the very beginning,

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:36.120
I still would have wanted my wish granted.

00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:40.250
I still would've gone down this road, all to become an Eternal Girl!

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:41.870
Go! Eagle!

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:48.590
<i>I would have been scared, but I'd still have done it.</i>

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:52.220
<i>I feel really sorry for Hitoe, but...</i>

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:56.640
<i>Her wish could have come true
without her becoming a Selector.</i>

00:15:57.510 --> 00:15:59.140
<i>My wish...</i>

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:02.560
<i>is a wish that could never come true, even if the world was destroyed.</i>

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:05.150
<i>A wish I couldn't make come true
without entering Selector battles.</i>

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:06.900
Yuzuki.

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:12.360
Your final attack, and your final oath.
We'll say it together.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.830
Now, let's say it together.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.460
I accept...

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:29.630
I... accept!

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.470
the Laws of the Selector.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:34.300
The Laws of the Selector.

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:35.090
And now!

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:39.220
A new Eternal Girl will be born!
A new Eternal Girl will be born!

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:42.310
Adamasphere!
Adamasphere!

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:52.950
It's happening?!

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:56.280
It's the birth of an Eternal Girl.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:07.630
Hanayo-san...

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:26.770
It's your long-awaited day off.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:29.150
Are you sure you don't want
to see your friends?

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.570
Y-Yeah.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:35.450
<i>Being with Grandma really relaxes me.</i>

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:41.330
<i>Battling is a whole lot of fun,
but I shouldn't get involved anymore.</i>

00:17:42.490 --> 00:17:43.200
<i>That...</i>

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:45.410
<i>That...</i>

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:47.420
<i>Let's not be friends anymore.</i>

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.590
Ruu-chan?

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:54.260
Ah, sorry. It's nothing.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:55.220
Really?

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:59.010
<i>I can't get involved anymore.</i>

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:05.060
Yes...

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:07.600
What the hell are you doing, leaving like that?!

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:11.980
Honoka-chan's fuming! She's saying you did something horrible to her!

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:15.650
I'll apologize with you, so you better come ba—

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.450
Girls are terrible.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.410
Yuzuki is nothing like them.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.080
<i>Yuzuki always has a smile on her face.</i>

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.960
<i>She doesn't put on a facade.</i>

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:31.840
<i>She keeps it to herself when things trouble her.</i>

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.840
<i>Like, doing it even though
you're brother and sister!</i>

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.590
What am I thinking?!

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:47.730
I'm back...

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.320
Yuzuki? What's the matter?

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.070
I just got dizzy there for a moment.

00:18:57.940 --> 00:18:59.450
Sorry, dinner...

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.700
You should lie down!

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:03.030
Can you walk?

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:03.870
Yeah.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:08.460
Thanks, Kazuki.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:09.920
It's fine.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.380
Did you put something on?

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:19.170
Like, a perfume...

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:20.720
Something smells pleasant.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:25.600
They say that if you think someone smells good,

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:28.310
you're attracted to that person on a genetic level.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:33.610
The one you're fated to be with... smells good.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.440
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:39.610
I mean, I've heard that too, but it can't be.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:42.610
That's only for people with
different genes to begin with.

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:44.450
Maybe we <i>are</i> that different.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:46.700
But we're twins.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:50.500
Maybe we were born with differences that were split between us.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.920
With this, we're one.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:00.670
Something's not right.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:01.510
What's not right?

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:04.430
You, and everyone else.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.930
Did something happen with the others?

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:11.770
I want you to talk about anything with me.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:15.860
I'm always on your side, Kazuki.

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.030
I'm eternally yours.

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:39.840
Can I come in?

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:44.430
Hitoe, did you eat?

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.390
You haven't eaten lunch either, have you?

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:50.720
You need to eat a bit at least...

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.560
Ah, right, Hitoe!

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:54.810
I have something good for you.

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.060
Here.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.610
You liked this, right?

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:04.950
I saw an ad about a new WIXOSS deck coming out, so I went and bought it.

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:07.700
Go ahead and take a look.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.240
Oh, I also bought a cake.

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:13.460
Maybe you'd rather eat something sweet.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:14.750
Let me go get it.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.580
Nice to meet you,

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:52.040
That
Oath
is
Falsehood

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:53.410
Selector.

00:21:53.410 --> 00:21:55.080
That
Oath
is
Falsehood

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:26.840
A card game?

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:28.380
The card did what?

00:23:28.380 --> 00:23:29.420
Wish...?

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:31.800
Did you spread it to everyone?

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:33.890
Thank you, Hanayo-san.

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:37.100
Do you remember me?

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:37.430
That
Truth
is
Cruel

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:40.060
That truth is cruel.

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:40.090
That
Truth
is
Cruel
